Three branches, three claims: shipments to the US are domestic, shipments to Canada or Mexico get a distinct label, everything else is international. That third branch, `else`, isn't neutral — it's a promise that every remaining country code the system will ever see belongs to exactly one bucket: 'international.' Is that actually true for this business, or did whoever wrote this just not think about, say, US territories that ship with different customs paperwork than the mainland?

